{
  "summary": "User Tom Becker (user_id 4, Finance) asked us to release a quarantined zip he thinks is a scan from the office copier. The only matching message is Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-08 08:26 UTC. It was quarantined as MALWARE and is not releasable. The sender is an external domain, not our internal copier, which looks like a common scan-themed malware lure. I did NOT release it. Security should review it and check whether other users got the same sender/subject. Separately, the account is locked after 5 failed password attempts on 2026-10-09 13:46\u201314:01 UTC. They all came from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York. There were no successful logins from unusual places, no hosting networks, and no Duo denials, so this looks like the user mistyping, not an attack. I have not queued an unlock because the user hasn't reported it. Still needed: security review of Q-1005, and checking whether the copier really sent anything (scan-to-email should come from an internal address).",
  "reason": "User wants a message marked malware released; per KB-007/KB-008 it cannot be released and needs security review"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the email you mean, \"Scanned document 0931.zip\". Our filter flagged it as malware, so I can't release it. It also came from an outside address (docs-share.example), not from our office copier. That's a common trick: fake scan emails with zip files attached. Please don't open or forward any copy of it. I've passed it to our security team to review. If you're waiting on a real scan, try sending it from the copier again. Real scans come from an internal address and should arrive normally. If they don't show up, reply here and we'll look into it. One more thing: your account is currently locked after several wrong password attempts this morning. If that's blocking you, let us know and we'll help you get back in.",
  "internal_note": "Quarantine has Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", reason malware, releasable=false. It was not released (KB-007/KB-008), and I escalated to Tier 2 for security review (escalation 1). The sender is external and not the internal copier, so this is likely a scan-themed malware lure. Unrelated: Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam) is also in quarantine, but the user didn't ask about it, so no action. The account is locked after 5 failed_password attempts on 10/09 09:46–10:01 ET from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10. No suspicious sign-ins, no hosting networks, no MFA denials. This looks like user error, so no unlock is queued until the user asks.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
